7px;\">20-35 m H</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">4-16</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">45-95%</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">0-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">0-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">0-0.43 (0.57)</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 121.817px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td style=\"height: 19px; width: 322.859px;\">Wood, Seeds, Resin</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 39px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 193.715px;\">Jolcham Oak</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 224.178px;\">Quercus serrata</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">20-25 m H</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">10-20</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">21-85%</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0.5-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0.3-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0.02-0.62 (0.76)</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 322.859px;\">Wood, Seeds, Tanin</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 39px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 193.715px;\">Windmill Palm</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 224.178px;\">Trachycarpus fortunei</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">12-20 m H</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">14-22</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">41-87%</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0.6-1</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">0.05-0.64 (0.72)</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 121.817px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td style=\"height: 39px; width: 322.859px;\">Rope, Firewood, Seeds</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler\">\n<div class=\"spoiler-toggle\">Compatibility</div>\n<div class=\"spoiler-text\"><a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/8785\">Biomes</a>: This mod adds plant life to the Central Palearctic, Eastern Palearctic, Pacific Palearctic, Australasian and Oceanic Realms<br /><a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/25902\">Soap and Lye: Bloom and Lather</a>: Crafting recipe to turn FZ Hibiscus into S&amp;L Hibiscus<br /><a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/wildcraftfruit\">Wildcraft</a>: Adds storage flags used by Wildcraft bags so FZ content can be added to WC bags<br /><a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/247\">XSkills</a>: Experience from berry bushes and trees<br /><br /></div>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler\">\n<div class=\"spoiler-toggle\">FAQ</div>\n<div class=\"spoiler-text\"><strong>Q:</strong> Why so many plant packs? Can't you make one giant one?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> The combined size of this series exceeds the Mod data base's file upload size limit and therefore could not be hosted on this site, making it extremely difficult for servers to use. What's more, I don't know just how large certain plant pack file sizes will get as new features come out and I want to ensure they don't need to be split in the future, as that may cause considerable server issues. Whenever mod packs are implemented, or if there are other resources for creating a more organized bundle, I will do so.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Q:</strong>&nbsp;Is this mod safe to add and remove to an existing world?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> It is safe to add, plants will only appear in chunks not previously generated. Removing this mod from an existing world will leave many broken blocks and is not recommended, but manually regenerating chunks via in game commands affecting can work.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Q:</strong> Can you add X plant?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> We are focusing on getting a core 30 plants into all 36 planned Floral Regions first before any plans to add more content, if ever. That said, we occasionally do commissions and would be open to adding plants that way. Check Tenth Architect's Discord or Author profile to see if any commission slots are open.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Q:</strong> Can you add X compatibility?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> Maintenance and our own planned content is our priority, and almost all our existing compatibilty files were those sent to us by community members. If you'd like to see compatibility added, you are welcome to make the patches, test to ensure they work and send them our way and we will add them. The exception to this would be if the size of the compatibility files would have significant performance impact for most users of this series, as performance is a higher priority of ours than cross compatibility.<br /><br /></div>\n</div>\n<p><br /><br />Features:</p>\n<p>The plants in this mod primarily spawn between 60 and 0 degrees latitude in a normal world climate.<br /><br />Links:<br /><a href=\"https://ko-fi.com/tentharchitect\">https://ko-fi.com/tentharchitect<br /><br /></a>A big thanks to everyone who gave feedback and assistance!</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> <br />All Rights Reserved. Please contact me if you are interested in making work derived from mine.</span></p>",
